#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# survival

#% text
# `survival(d, x)` gives the survival function `P(X > x) = 1 - cdf(d, x)`, computed so that it stays accurate far in the upper tail.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
survival(exponential_distribution(l), x)
#% output
#= piecewise([[exp(-l*x), x >= 0]], 1)

#% cell
survival(normal_distribution(0, 1), 1.96)
#% output
#= 0.024997895148220435

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Deep in the tail, `1 - cdf` loses everything to cancellation:

#% cell
[survival(normal_distribution(0, 1), 10.0), 1 - cdf(normal_distribution(0, 1), 10.0)]
#% output
#= [7.619853024160523e-24, 0.0]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `cdf`, `quantile`, `erfc`
